# DTF tier manifest: age-gate-repo-admin  (artifact-keeper#4238, PR #4239)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. Like age-gate-review-reopen, the held
# versions come from proxying the real `is-odd` packument from
# registry.npmjs.org (egress required). The gate runs in `first_seen` mode,
# so on a fresh stack every version is "young" and held (7 reviews per repo),
# independent of how old the upstream releases are.
#
# THE FEATURE (#4238, merged as #4239 / ae91da02, migration 290, milestone 1.12.0)
# The age gate was configured per repository but operable only by an instance
# admin. Now a principal holding the fine-grained `repository:admin` action
# (permissions table: principal, group, or project inheritance) on a
# repository can, for THAT repository only:
#   GET/PUT /api/v1/repositories/{key}/age-gate
#   GET     /api/v1/repositories/{key}/age-gate/reviews[/{id}]   (filter from
#           the path; ?repository_key= ignored; another repo's id -> 404)
#   POST    /api/v1/repositories/{key}/age-gate/reviews/{id}/{approve|reject|reopen}
# Responses name the decider (reviewed_by_username, _is_service_account).
# Migration 290 adds the instance-admin lock: an instance-admin policy write
# (unless it sends instance_locked:false) and an instance-admin review decision
# are locked; a repository admin may tighten but not disable, lower, re-mode
# or unlock a locked policy, and may reject but not approve or reopen a locked
# review. Audit: REPOSITORY_UPDATED details.age_gate_change{actor_tier,
# relaxed,...}, AGE_GATE_APPROVED/REJECTED/REOPENED details.actor_tier,
# AGE_GATE_LOCK_SET / AGE_GATE_LOCK_RELEASED {lock: policy|review}.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   Two public remote npm repos A and B on registry.npmjs.org; a non-admin
#   user U granted [admin] on A through POST /api/v1/permissions; nothing on B.
#   "served" = the version key is present in a fresh proxied packument.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)     U reads and enables A's gate (stored unlocked); U lists A's
#             pending reviews (A only, also with ?repository_key=B), reads one,
#             a B review id through A's route is 404 for GET and approve, an
#             unknown decision is 400; U approves one (released in the
#             packument, reviewed_by_username U, unlocked) and the /admin queue
#             shows it approved by U; an instance-admin reject locks a review
#             (U approve/reopen 403); an instance-admin policy write locks A
#             (U lower/disable/re-mode/unlock 403, policy unchanged; tighten
#             200); the instance admin hands both back and U may then relax and
#             approve; audit rows carry actor and tier. RED on 1.11.3 (U gets
#             403 "Admin access required" on A's gate, no scoped queue).
#   (CONTROL) both images: instance-admin PUT/GET of B's gate, the hold, the
#             /admin queue, approve releases and reject re-blocks the version;
#             U is refused (403/404) on every B gate and queue route and on the
#             instance queue, and B's policy and review do not change.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~60 calls back to back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
